WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Hakone Ekiden Memories</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.940
<b>Spun along with the runner's sash</b>

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.570
<i>Spun along with the runner's
sash are numerous dramas.</i>

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.860
<b>Numerous dramas</b>

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.320
<b>Dead heats between aces.</b>

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>Dead heats between aces.</i>

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.450
<i>This is the moment a new legend
was born during the second section.</i>

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.740
<i>As temperatures rose during the fourth
section, there was an accident.</i>

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.750
<i>A coach's words saved a runner.</i>

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.030
<i>On the steep slopes of Mt. Hakone...</i>

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.620
It's well-edited.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.640
My heart naturally begins to leap.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.340
On January 2nd and 3rd of next year, 
we'll be there this time.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.720
Each of us will stand on his own
starting line and wait for the sash.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.340
We'll receive it and 
pass it on to the next man.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.900
Passing it on again and again, 
we'll eventually meet again at Otemachi.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.340
It will be the Kansei University Long Distance
Track Team's first major accomplishment.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.770
No, it will be the first time in recent history

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:00.790
that a team makes it 
to the Ekiden on their first try.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.250
That's all.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.390
Do you guys feel a little closer now...

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.040
...to the Hakone Ekiden?

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.520
<b>Volume</b>

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.520
<b>Hakone Ekiden Memories</b>

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.420
What's wrong with you? It's too loud!

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.320
We're watching it again!
You can never watch this too many times!

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.570
Don't talk to me about New Year's!

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.530
Summer! It's summer right now!

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.030
On January 2nd and 3rd of next year, 
we'll be there this time.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.990
Each of us will stand on his own
starting line and wait for—

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:55.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>Recruitment Examination
Interview Room</b>

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.250
Excuse me.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:17.760
You're quite tan.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.460
Yes, sir.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.980
I've been training.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.680
Training?

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.640
I'm hoping to run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:38.400
Why is he chasing me?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.670
He's like a fish in water.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.120
But we're in the mountains.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:52.730
We got one.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.090
<b><i>Fan Club Formed</i></b>

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:58.090
That's our 30th fan club application.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.700
We've been getting more
since we put up the website.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.650
Yeah.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.140
It's because the website you made is so good.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.050
That's not it.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.020
It's because the photos you take are so good.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.400
Musa...

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.860
We can't keep up with him on the flats.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:26.910
What?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.370
There's no way that's true.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.040
I'm serious.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.210
I tried selling them to 
a general store, and look.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:38.540
<b>Super Popular <3 For Good Luck
Nico Nico Dolls
We're on Social Media</b>

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.390
Huh.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:38.540
They're really popular. I'm making a profit.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.260
Nico Nico?

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.630
You know it's nico for nicotine, right?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.040
It doesn't matter what they're called.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.090
Do you think you could increase production?

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.130
It's not like I ever put
much thought into them.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.280
I'll mention them on our website.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.870
Should we do online sales?

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.060
Do whatever you want.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.700
In other words,

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:13.580
we need to match everyone's strengths
to each 20-kilometer section, right?

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.120
A team like ours has no choice
but to focus on that.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.340
Yeah. I'm planning to switch over
to running in 10K races, too.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.050
We need to increase our distance, starting with those
who have achieved the requisite time.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.790
I've been reading a few books
on long distance running.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.100
Hey.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.820
We're gonna start lighting them.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.220
Ta-da!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.080
We're coming.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.420
I'd like to understand the goals
of our training schedule better.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.930
I have a few suggestions. Let's talk later.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:43.830
Got it.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:49.140
Yuki understands the scientific
stuff better than I do.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.950
That's why I made him a member.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.620
Did you really?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.870
Last spurt!

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.840
Prince, your time improved again!

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.790
Don't you feel like practice is fun?

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:10.910
Yeah.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.010
I guess it's because we went through
that hellish Lake Shirakaba experience.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.730
We're really running, aren't we?

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.980
Maybe we'll run right past
Hakone all the way to Mt. Fuji.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.370
There's nothing everyone else
can do that you can't do.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.580
Fight on—

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.120
What?

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.030
Eight 5000-meter runs?

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.600
That's practically a full marathon!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.450
I want to go back to Tokyo!

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:42.150
You'll be strong enough
to run back in another week.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.880
Don't give me that bullshit.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.340
Don't worry.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.300
We'll be dumping plenty of water on you.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.010
Promise me you'll let me 
onto the truck before I die.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.790
Good luck.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:56.420
Go!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.350
Here. It's on the house.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.150
<b>Fresh Meat
Kobori Butcher Shop</b>

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.150
What? This is too much.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:06.070
<b>Kobori Butcher Shop</b>

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.730
I heard about you.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.070
You're nationally competitive, right?

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.530
You need to keep future stars in your debt.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.060
I'm impressed.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.760
Huh?

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.480
You're still growing.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.190
Your muscles feel different.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.060
You must be getting good practice.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.530
Yeah.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.740
Everyone will achieve an official record.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.960
We'll participate in and naturally
make it through the qualifier.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:05.420
Our only goal is the peak of Hakone.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.670
The actual race involves
running back down, though.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.050
We're still on the way there.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.880
We can become even stronger.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.980
The mountains of Hakone are?

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.340
The steepest in the world!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.120
Hey, cut that out!

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:39.030
Be careful!

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:42.870
It's falling!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.540
Here we go!

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.050
Damn.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:03.950
Huh?

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.820
Look at how hard they're working.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.180
Don't you want them to make it, no matter what?

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.050
Yeah.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.290
But there are plenty of other guys out there

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.800
who are working just as hard.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.190
Probably.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:21.370
It's just running, though. It's insane.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.170
It's kind of frustrating that
all we can do is watch.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.130
Yeah. That's why I said “damn.”

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.090
Dad, I want to go to Kansei University.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.980
Say something.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:44.980
Like what? Damn it?

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.940
<b><i>You're Not Alone</i></b>

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:14.900
Want to head up to the summit
before we return to Tokyo?

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:15.990
What?

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.260
You want to do more training?

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.570
No.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:23.810
Let's see the view together
to cap off this training camp.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:54.050
I thought views were something
I'd enjoy once I was old.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.300
I know what you mean.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.000
But it's kind of nice.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.010
Yeah.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.150
Have we gotten used to the outdoors?

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:03.530
Is that why?

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.990
It's because we're viewing it together.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:11.450
I doubt we'd feel this way
if we viewed it alone.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:15.570
I agree.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.280
What feeling are you talking about?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.710
You're starting to say
some pretty witty things.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.080
Hey, that's right.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.340
Didn't he say he wanted
to become a better speaker

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.120
when we were drinking the other day?

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.830
Yeah, he did.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:33.390
I guess people do grow.

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:34.890
What's wrong with you guys?

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.760
We're friends running the same path together.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.560
No one's alone anymore.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:46.430
Yeah.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.190
Let's head back. The real battle starts now.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:55.860
<b>Dochido University Track Meet</b>

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:06.950
See you at the finish line.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:35.690
<i>Huh?</i>

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.610
<i>I'm not alone.</i>

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.000
Nico-chan Senpai!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.570
Go!

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.240
King!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.030
You can do it!

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:52.700
Go, go, go, go!

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.550
Yes!

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.780
<b>Boso University Track</b>

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:24.490
All runners participating in the 5000-meter
race, please gather at the starting line.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:29.730
All runners participating in the 5000-meter
race, please gather at the starting line.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.420
See you later.

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.260
We'll block the wind for you.

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.750
If I can keep up.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.080
You will.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.180
The temperature's cool today.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:45.800
Your times are good overall.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.700
It's not about the order in which you finish.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.180
It's a race against time. Against yourself.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.910
What's this? Have you always been a runner?

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.140
Shut up!

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.770
Next time, next time!

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.980
You've got plenty more chances!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.330
<b>Yamato University Field</b>

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.330
<b>Yamato University Student Center</b>

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.030
His times are definitely improving, though.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.560
<b>Yamato Uni</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>September</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>Boso Uni</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>Yamato Uni</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>Tokyo Sport Uni</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>October</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>Entry Deadline</b>

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.190
<b>Qualifier</b>

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.480
<b>Qualifier</b>

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:47.780
<b>Entry Deadline</b>

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.660
<b>Tokyo Sport Uni</b>

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.040
I'm just going for a short run.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.230
I'll go with you.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:08.460
You don't have to. Aren't you taking a bath?

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.400
I want to run, too.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.480
I'll go with you.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:15.930
You're a freak, aren't you?

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.140
What?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:22.100
<b>Hngh</b>

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.600
Don't worry. Go on.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.300
It's just a short jog.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.660
It's something I do occasionally.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:16:01.220
Doesn't sitting in the water in the dark
make you feel incredibly uneasy?

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:05.830
Doing it deliberately makes me
feel like I can reexamine myself.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.760
It's like meditating.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:08.910
Ah.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:13.360
I see. Prince went running alone?

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.970
Should I have gone with him?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.730
Leaving a person alone
can be kindness as well.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:26.810
It's okay. Even if he runs alone, he's not alone.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.730
Haiji said the same thing.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:30.770
What?

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:32.510
He told me that a while ago.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.720
That no matter how much you
run alone, you're not actually alone.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.320
Running is fun, isn't it?

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.870
It's just running, but I've
learned all kinds of things.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:45.770
Yeah.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:47.860
Oh, right.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:51.250
Huh?

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:55.630
Since you're always in the front,
you probably haven't noticed,

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.870
but recently I made a wonderful discovery.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.140
A discovery? What is it?

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:02.410
What should I do?

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.130
Oh, how wonderful it is to be young.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:10.370
What is it? It's dark, and we're naked.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.480
Hey, look.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:16.180
I thought it was a streetlight,
but it's the moon.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.300
I caught it in my hands.

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:22.020
What's going on with you?

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:26.560
<b>Tokyo Sport University</b>

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.940
Um, do you have a moment?

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.050
You really are interested in them.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.620
They might not even make it
to the qualifier, though.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:01.860
Excuse me.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.070
You're not going to stand with him?

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.970
You don't want to pressure him?

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.070
He'll feel it no matter where I am.

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:21.540
How much time do you think
we've spent together?

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:29.270
I'm jealous of them that
they have you to say that.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.180
Prince! Go, go!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.180
Prince! Prince!

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.660
Um, do you have a moment?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.540
If there's something you want to say,

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.930
you can write it here.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.680
<i>Unbelievable. When they look at me like that...</i>

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.870
<b>Forward!!</b>

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.070
<i>...how could I not...</i>

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.290
<i>...do my best?</i>

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:56.750
<b>Forward!!</b>

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.150
<i>Forward!</i>

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:58.890
<i>Forward!</i>

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.490
<i>Forward!</i>

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.340
<i>Forward!</i>

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:05.180
<b>Forward!!</b>

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.320
<i>Forward!</i>

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.520
Prince!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:39.600
Now we all have official records!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.630
We made it to the qualifier!

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.840
<b>Forward!!</b>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:45.920
Next time: Place of Destiny

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:42.920
<b>Next time: “Place of Destiny.”</b>
